+## Threshold Validation
+
+The `frai eval` command supports optional `--threshold` flags to gate CI pipelines on metric scores:
+- Format: `--threshold <metric_id>=<min_value>` (repeatable)
+- Valid metric IDs: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance` (plus custom metrics)
+- Threshold value must be between 0 and 1
+- A metric with null score (unable to compute) fails its threshold
+- Exit codes:
+  - 0: All thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)
+  - 1: Any threshold fails
+  - 2: Malformed threshold or unknown metric (no report written)
+- Reports are generated regardless of pass/fail and include `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields
+- SDK users can pass `thresholds` to `Eval.generateReport()`
+
+Example:
+```bash
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=1.0
+```
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
